WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.222 --> 00:00:14.604
Daniel was eating lunch with his grandmother and her friends at the retirement community.

2
00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:21.306
"Daniel does wonderful magic tricks," Grandma said proudly to Mr.

3
00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:22.286
Hudson and Mrs.

4
00:00:22.386 --> 00:00:25.547
Ross. "Would you like to see one?"

5
00:00:26.727 --> 00:00:29.208
Daniel picked up his spoon and wiped it off.

6
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:35.951
"I will now use my magic powers to bend this spoon."

7
00:00:41.035 --> 00:00:44.978
Daniel focused on the spoon, which slowly bent in his hands.

8
00:00:51.043 --> 00:00:52.183
a clever boy!"

9
00:00:52.424 --> 00:00:53.344
Grandma said.

10
00:00:55.446 --> 00:00:56.026
But Mr.

11
00:00:56.086 --> 00:00:57.768
Hudson wasn't impressed.

12
00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:02.567
"You need to work on concealing the spoon's handle.

13
00:01:07.511 --> 00:01:11.615
A magician must be aware of how his tricks look from every angle.

14
00:01:13.497 --> 00:01:15.879
I could see what you were doing over here."

15
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.180
Daniel sighed.

16
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.323
"Are you a magician?"

17
00:01:22.644 --> 00:01:24.025
Mr. Hudson nodded.

18
00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:26.908
"What's your favorite trick?"

19
00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:29.777
Daniel's face lit up.

20
00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:35.239
"I love all kinds of magic, especially big illusions!

21
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.161
It would be fun to make someone float above a table."

22
00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:48.425
tricks require special equipment that amateur magicians don't have," Mr.

23
00:01:48.465 --> 00:01:49.346
Hudson said.

24
00:01:49.366 --> 00:01:53.848
"Things like platforms that rise in the air.

25
00:01:56.696 --> 00:02:01.638
But I think card tricks and other close-up magic require more skill."

26
00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:04.159
He took out a coin.

27
00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:11.162
"My favorite tricks involve teleportation—like moving coins from place to place."

28
00:02:12.082 --> 00:02:15.364
Mr. Hudson made the coin vanish from one hand.

29
00:02:16.304 --> 00:02:19.685
He pulled it out from behind Daniel's ear with his other hand.

30
00:02:22.547 --> 00:02:23.747
Daniel shook his head.

31
00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.728
"How did you do that?"

32
00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:29.625
"Practice!" Mr.

33
00:02:29.685 --> 00:02:30.505
Hudson winked.

34
00:02:32.526 --> 00:02:38.288
"I've always admired escape artists, though their routines make me so nervous," Mrs.

35
00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:39.029
Ross said.

36
00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:44.171
"Especially when someone is handcuffed or tied inside a tank of water."

37
00:02:44.191 --> 00:02:47.532
"Don't worry," Mr.

38
00:02:47.572 --> 00:02:48.352
Hudson said.

39
00:02:48.372 --> 00:02:56.536
"An assistant slips the magician the keys to the handcuffs or uses knots that are easy to untie.

40
00:02:58.588 --> 00:03:02.451
The magician escapes quickly but stays underwater for suspense."

41
00:03:05.794 --> 00:03:08.055
"I still wouldn't want Daniel trying that!"

42
00:03:08.456 --> 00:03:09.376
Grandma said.

43
00:03:09.396 --> 00:03:14.360
"I prefer classic tricks like pulling a rabbit out of a hat."

44
00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:19.104
"Nobody does that anymore, Grandma.

45
00:03:21.606 --> 00:03:24.508
Using animals in magic acts is considered cruel.

46
00:03:26.196 --> 00:03:29.978
Magicians pull other things out of hats today—like bowling balls!"

47
00:03:29.998 --> 00:03:35.642
"The item is often hidden in a secret compartment," Mr.

48
00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:36.742
Hudson explained.

49
00:03:36.762 --> 00:03:44.207
"The magician sets his hat over the compartment and pulls the object through an opening in the hat."

50
00:03:44.227 --> 00:03:47.969
"I'm just a beginner," Daniel said.

51
00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:52.212
"All those tricks take lots of practice!"

52
00:03:53.472 --> 00:03:55.914
Daniel was determined to outwit Mr.

53
00:03:55.954 --> 00:04:03.800
Hudson. So the next time he visited Grandma, he brought an assistant, his friend Joaquin.

54
00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:11.466
"There's another kind of magic we didn't discuss," Daniel said as Joaquin blindfolded him.

55
00:04:11.486 --> 00:04:13.768
"Mind reading."

56
00:04:13.788 --> 00:04:16.230
Joaquin invited Mrs.

57
00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.912
Ross to hand him any item from her purse.

58
00:04:22.608 --> 00:04:25.050
"I'm thinking about this object."

59
00:04:25.491 --> 00:04:26.631
Joaquin paused.

60
00:04:29.053 --> 00:04:29.874
"Read my mind."

61
00:04:29.894 --> 00:04:33.717
"Wallet," Daniel said.

62
00:04:33.737 --> 00:04:37.260
"You're right!"

63
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.222
Mrs. Ross handed Joaquin something else.

64
00:04:40.242 --> 00:04:44.306
"I'm thinking about this object."

65
00:04:45.527 --> 00:04:47.568
Joaquin paused for a few seconds.

66
00:04:50.591 --> 00:04:51.912
"Read my mind."

67
00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.341
"Comb," Daniel replied.

68
00:05:02.103 --> 00:05:03.424
Mr. Hudson applauded.

69
00:05:03.444 --> 00:05:11.807
"Magicians and their assistants usually have code words for different items, but I'm puzzled.

70
00:05:13.168 --> 00:05:15.649
Joaquin said the same thing both times.

71
00:05:17.029 --> 00:05:20.831
If you did the trick again, I could probably figure it out."

72
00:05:21.891 --> 00:05:23.752
Daniel removed his blindfold.

73
00:05:26.928 --> 00:05:28.751
"That's why we're not repeating it!"

74
00:05:29.111 --> 00:05:29.632
he said.

75
00:05:29.652 --> 00:05:34.157
"Won't you read my mind just once?"

76
00:05:34.558 --> 00:05:35.539
Grandma pleaded.

77
00:05:35.559 --> 00:05:39.424
"Sure, that's easy."

78
00:05:40.405 --> 00:05:41.246
Daniel grinned.

79
00:05:41.266 --> 00:05:45.331
"You're thinking, 'Such a clever boy!'"
